  "notes": [
    "Can recreate formations that crossed into Russia, Lithuanian forces raised on liberation, and the 'Bug Division'.",
    "1 to 2 Infantry Brigades: 1 or 2 Regiments of Polish Infantry (1-4 battalions), plus 0 to 2 Chasseur/Jäger battalions (Lithuanians and Bug Division).",
    "0 to 1 Regimental Artillery section per 3 battalions, or 0 to 1 Regimental Artillery battery per infantry regiment of 3+ battalions.",
    "0 to 1 Cavalry Brigade (1 per 2 Infantry Brigades): 1 or 2 regiments from up to 1 Hussar, up to 6 Uhlan, up to 3 Chasseur-à-Cheval (army-wide caps).",
    "Divisional Artillery: 0 to 2 Foot Artillery batteries (1 per 7 battalions).",
    "Reserve Artillery: up to 1 Horse battery (if 8 battalions taken) and up to 1 Heavy Foot battery (if 8 battalions taken), attached to any brigade.",
    "Allies: a Polish army can take 25% allies from any single allied list."
  ]
